@node aec Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Acoustic Echo Cancellation plugin — PBFDAF with two-path and post-filter.

@subsubheading What It Does

Removes echo from audio streams in real-time. When a microphone picks up audio playing through speakers, the AEC plugin subtracts the known playback signal to produce clean microphone audio. Uses a Partitioned Block Frequency Domain Adaptive Filter (PBFDAF) for efficient cancellation.

@subsubheading Features

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{PBFDAF algorithm}: Efficient frequency-domain adaptive filtering
@item @strong{Two-path architecture}: Robust convergence with separate foreground/background filters
@item @strong{Post-filter}: Residual echo suppression for additional cleanup
@item @strong{Real-time processing}: Low-latency operation suitable for live audio
@end itemize


